# Parallel ledger appends must AUTO-UNION, never conflict.
#
# docs/DECISIONS.md is append-only (ruling 26) and is touched by nearly every
# lane. Two lanes that each append a new row to the end of the table produce a
# textual merge conflict on the shared tail line under git's default 3-way
# merge — a class that has hit every parallel-pair (~3x). `merge=union` tells
# git to keep BOTH sides' added lines instead of conflicting, so parallel
# appends combine automatically.
#
# The ONE failure union-merge can introduce — two lanes independently claiming
# the SAME row id — is caught by the dup-slug lint in
# scripts/check-decision-guards.cjs, which runs in CI (build.yml
# decision-guards-lint job) and fails on a duplicate id of any shape
# (numeric OR date-slug). Union-merge + dup-slug-lint is the pair: the driver
# removes the conflict, the lint catches the only bad merge it could produce.
# Proven by scripts/check-ledger-union-merge.cjs --self-test (ledger-union job).
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union
